findings.body:
**IDOR: any authenticated user can read any account.**

`body.accountId` is trusted whenever it is present. A normal user can POST `{"accountId":"<victim>"}` and receive that account’s record. The support-tools comment does not enforce staff-only access.

Require an explicit staff/support authorization check before accepting a client-supplied id, and keep the default path as `caller.accountId` only:

```typescript
const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
let id = caller.accountId;
if (body.accountId != null) {
  if (!caller.isSupportStaff) { // or whatever role flag auth() provides
    return Response.json({ error: "forbidden" }, { status: 403 });
  }
  id = body.accountId;
}
```

Also confirm this route’s method: reading `req.json()` on a GET is unreliable in many runtimes; staff tools should use a dedicated staff route or a validated query/body on an allowed method.
